(globalThis.CATALOGUE_RECORD_CHUNKS??=Object.create(null))[140]={"source_order":140,"notes":["The show-through is reversed and very faint. I cannot fully exclude a very faint original pencil mark, but on inspection of all native tiles every visible trace matches the mirrored recto layout.","The faint, mirror-reversed writing across the whole page is show-through from the recto, fol. 70. It is visible in the adjacent context image: entries Gopālasahasranāmāvali through Gorakṣaśataka and the shelfmarks d. 670(4) through d. 458(4). It is not target-page text and is not transcribed as blocks.","The left-hand stacked edges are the edges of other leaves in the gathering. The ruled lines carry no original writing on this verso.","I reviewed the overview and all six native tiles. The page has no original catalogue writing: no holdings, headings, cross-references or marginal or bottom notes.","The only original mark is the pencil folio number at the top left. It is written '70' with a superscript 'b', at approx. bbox [415,305,140,140], and is recorded as visible_folio. It is not catalogue text, so no record was created for it.","The faint, mirror-reversed writing across the ruled area is show-through from the recto, fol. 70 (source order 139). Its layout matches that page: shelfmark column at left, dates such as '1881: 20:7:D' at right, and the bottom note 'Text is on ff. 12-33' reversed near the foot. It was not transcribed as target-page text.","The page also shows non-writing physical features. A binding thread loop runs along the right/gutter edge (approx. [3200,660,60,900]). There are dark specks at the left edge (approx. [330,1050,60,200]) and a small diagonal smudge in the lower middle (approx. [2140,3870,120,60]). The stacked leaf edges at left and the printed ruling carry no writing.","A very faint original pencil trace cannot be wholly excluded beneath the show-through. However, every visible trace inspected matches the mirrored layout of fol. 70.","Faint dash-like strokes and wavy marks near the bottom centre-left could not be securely matched to the mirrored recto layout. They are most likely show-through, set-off from fol. 71, or a stain. A faint original pencil mark cannot be wholly excluded, but none of the traces forms legible text."],"records":[]};
